    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are leaning into speed and favorable matchups today, with **Trea Turner** (75.89) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (72.94) serving as our primary offensive engines. **Trea Turner** occupies the prime leadoff spot against Dollander, bolstered by the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which provides a significant boost to his elite stolen base potential. Similarly, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is a high-conviction start; despite the lower lineup position, his aggressive dynamic platoon advantage against the opposing right-hander and a perfect 100% success rate factor for stolen bases against the current mound matchup make him a cornerstone for our 5x5 Roto requirements. **Kyle Schwarber** also warrants attention at 69.70; his xwOBA profile and high-order placement provide a strong floor despite the neutral-to-tough pitching environment.\n\nWhile we remain opportunistic, our lineup construction prioritizes efficiency over raw volume. **Junior Caminero** (56.98) and **Yordan Alvarez** (57.92) headline our secondary tier of strong starts, both benefiting from favorable park factors and the chance to drive in runs despite facing some stiff competition from Early and Lodolo. The most difficult personnel decision centered on **Hyeseong Kim**, who landed just outside our threshold at 36.57. While **Hyeseong Kim** carries value, the optimizer ultimately pivoted away due to a high-difficulty matchup against Sale, where the lefty-on-lefty penalty proved too restrictive to justify a spot over our primary starters. \n\nWe are monitoring several \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Gary Sanchez**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Colt Keith**, and **Pete Crow-Armstrong**; please ensure these players are confirmed in their projected slots as the official reports surface. We have opted for caution with **Caleb Durbin**, whose score of 44.21 suggests a marginal start. While he lacks an elite projection, the benefit of an \"Out\" wind factor and his role in the lineup provides just enough padding to keep him in the mix. Owners should note that **Christian Yelich**, **Zac Veen**, **Lars Nootbaar**, **Josh Smith**, **Pedro Ramirez**, and **Luis Pena** are currently unavailable due to injury or roster status, necessitating the current depth configuration.",
